In this task, we are given a set of points and a target ratio for each parent group (demographic group) that the children should be represented in the fair sample. The goal is to construct a weighted fair geometric hitting set under both demographic parity constraints (DP) and custom-ratio (CR) constraints.

The problem involves creating a fair geometric hitting set, which means selecting a subset of ranges such that each parent group's proportion within an ϵmargin margin is preserved in the sample. The Parent has to construct this weighted fair \ud835\udf00-sample under both demographic parity (DP) and custom-ratio (CR) constraints, which are more complex than simple demographic parity (DP).

The parent's task is to create a Python function that takes in input the number of children `n`, the list of all possible target ratios for each child group as an array of tuples `(a_i, b_i)` where $a_i$ and $b_i$ are integers representing the lower and upper bounds respectively. The parent should also provide a counterexample illustrating this limitation in the technical report [32].

The fair geometric hitting set problem is an optimization problem that involves selecting a subset of points from a range space such that each demographic group's proportion within an ϵmargin margin is preserved, while satisfying certain constraints. The parent has to create a weighted fair \ud835\udf00-sample under both demographic parity (DP) and custom-ratio (CR) constraints by extending the techniques introduced for \ud835\udc42(\ud835\udc61)-nets. 

The fair geometric hitting set problem is a generalization of the classic hitting set problem, where we aim to select a subset of points from a range space that satisfies certain constraints on the representation ratios of different demographic groups within an \ud835\udf00margin. The parent has to create a weighted fair geometric hitting set under both demographic parity (DP) and custom-ratio (CR) constraints by extending the techniques introduced for \ud835\udc42(\ud835\udc61)-nets. 

The problem is addressed in this paper, which presents a formal argument and provides a counterexample illustrating this limitation in the technical report [32]. The parent should also provide one-line comments on how to address this issue.
